se their melodies  everything that we're touching designing  is top to bottom  carvers students to carver alum down to  the t-shirts and everything  they call the label what else carver  records  when they played me the music i was  shocked and so i sent it out to a couple  people in the industry  i didn't say this is a high school  project i'm working on you just sent it  to him  like what do you think of this yeah and  then he's like can we sign them i'm like  well they're in high school he's like oh  we are definitely going to do this the  crew doesn't have a recording contract  yet but by the end of summer they plan  to release  three singles and an album does this  kind of change your trajectory  i feel like it opened my eyes to the  possibilities of the music business  it also earned caleb a full scholarship  to study the industry  at drexel university this fall what's  the feeling you get when you hear  this single finished it's just like wow  all the hard work we put in this just  all came together maybe the fame  won't be too far off  for cbs this morning christina rothini  philadelphia  now we want to know the name of that  song yes caleb  the group doesn't even have a name yet i  love it i love the logo carver records  but i love what they're doing and how  they're doing it  you can see their passion and enthusiasm  and not for nothing they're good  yeah they are and they're giving me the  new edition fields right caleb  18 years old he did he producer  yeah i like that i like that little  motto their heart can only take you so  far  that is so true right
 

